{start_of_verse}
[Am]Iron kettle on the [C]stove again
[G]Whistling like it know[Am]s where I have been
[Am]Morning paper that I [C]never read
[G]Headlines piling up bes[Am]ide the bed
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]Pour me one [C]more, pour me slow
[G]Ain't no place I[Am]'ve got to go
[F]Pour me one [C]more, let it steep
[G]Till the world g[Am]oes back to sleep
{end_of_chorus}

